==English==
{{rfc}}

===Etymology===
Seems to have originated from a phrase by [[w:Manute Bol|Manute Bol]], a player of Sudanese origin for the [[w:Golden State Warriors|Golden State Warriors]] [[basketball]] team in California. Subsequently adopted by other players.

===Interjection===
{{en-intj|pos=my bad}} 

# {{colloquial}} {{idiomatic}} My fault; [[mea culpa]].
#: ''Yes, I realize the humvee isn't supposed to be parked in the heirloom flowerbed. '''My bad'''.''

